  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "LF9r7NQyW76gQoUDCfL/SlOxKMY=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:33.821Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "BJSS was acquired by CGI in January 2025. The research states the consequence in the pilot's own terms: the UK's largest independent engineering consultancy left the independent pool. Its tool field now reads, literally, \"now CGI's stack\".\n\nThat phrase is the mechanism. Platform selection after an acquisition of this kind consolidates at group level, so the firm scored for its independence and its public, NHS and banking verticals no longer owns the decision being sold to. The verticals remain attractive and are now reachable only through a much larger organisation's standards process.\n\nRead alongside its neighbours, this row is part of a trend rather than an isolated event: SDC into Netcompany, Centric into the Imker Capital consortium, BJSS into CGI, Ibermatica into Ayesa. The pool of independent mid-market integrators this brief targets is actively shrinking, which is a finding about the market's structure and not merely about BJSS. The row itself remains a provisional v2 tail entry with an OSS-portfolio screen still outstanding.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- BJSS (UK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> \u26a0 M&A: acquired by CGI (Jan-2025). The UK's largest independent engineering consultancy left the independent pool. \u00b7 DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Public, healthcare (NHS), banking",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:33.821894Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:33.821898Z"
    }
  },
